      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. to be more specific, im seeing a lot of movement in the north and west districts. the north district is stayin pretty much the same in terms of demographic makeup, mostly white middle-class families, while the west district is seeing a much faster increase in ethnic diversity and immigrant populations. from a purely economic standpoint, which of these trends is a better indicator of long-term stability for property values? i want to avoid areas that might see a drop in demand due to rapid social or demographic shifts.",
